From 7b3596636b49f9737f712c02650f096517101cdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 09:23:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07389/11362] [outer-loop] adversarial_verify: recognize
 web_and_bibliographic_search_only substrate

Two source-delta/SOTA-ingestion artifacts overnight (exp5718 v511, exp5732 v512)
were flagged DURATION_TOO_SHORT despite declaring
inference_substrate=web_and_bibliographic_search_only -- pure WebSearch/WebFetch
+ a research-references.md read, genuinely fast, no model load. The linter
simply didn't recognize that substrate value, so it fell through to the 60s
live_llm_inference floor whenever the ingested literature happened to mention
GGUF/CUDA in prose. Confirmed via two sibling v510/v513 ingestion artifacts with
the same substrate that passed clean (their content didn't trip the marker
detector) -- a substrate-recognition gap, not artifact-specific fabrication.

Adds WEB_BIBLIOGRAPHIC_SEARCH_ONLY_SUBSTRATE with a 0.0001s floor, following the
exact pattern of the existing deterministic_smt_hint_validation_no_llm /
artifact_qa_lint_tests substrates. Deliberately does NOT touch exp5718's own
separate flag (duration_s=2.7e-07, 270ns -- implausible for any task involving a
WebSearch network round-trip regardless of substrate); loosening the floor
further to paper over that would be gaming the linter, not fixing the gap. New
test file reproduces both the fix and the correctly-still-flagged case with the
real triggering content (GGUF-mentioning prose) from both artifacts. Full
adversarial_verify test suite: 340 passed, 5 skipped (pre-existing, unrelated
missing-optional-dependency skips), 0 failures.

